1
00:00:12,721 --> 00:00:14,973
<i>Baran, is this you?</i>

2
00:00:20,562 --> 00:00:23,314
It began after a bad case
of viral meningitis

3
00:00:23,315 --> 00:00:25,107
when I was five.

4
00:00:25,108 --> 00:00:27,443
They tried every
anti-seizure medication,

5
00:00:27,444 --> 00:00:31,405
but I still had episodes
every few months or so.

6
00:00:31,406 --> 00:00:32,615
No one's ever noticed before.

7
00:00:32,616 --> 00:00:34,076
They just think I'm thoughtful.

8
00:00:36,119 --> 00:00:37,578
Are you driving?

9
00:00:37,579 --> 00:00:40,665
I couldn't
until laser ablation

10
00:00:40,666 --> 00:00:44,001
to my left temporal lobe
12 years ago.

11
00:00:44,002 --> 00:00:46,837
Between that and the Keppra,
I've been seizure-free,

12
00:00:46,838 --> 00:00:50,467
cleared by Neurology to drive
and to work as an attending.

13
00:00:52,302 --> 00:00:54,595
How long, uh,
between the seizure

14
00:00:54,596 --> 00:00:56,472
you had today and the last one?

15
00:00:56,473 --> 00:00:59,685
It's been well over a year.

16
00:01:01,895 --> 00:01:03,272
But I had two today.

17
00:01:07,985 --> 00:01:09,527
I don't know why.

18
00:01:09,528 --> 00:01:12,780
It could be sleep deprivation,
new job stress.

19
00:01:12,781 --> 00:01:16,033
I--I haven't had to deal
with Peds cases

20
00:01:16,034 --> 00:01:17,577
since Afghanistan.

21
00:01:17,578 --> 00:01:19,328
What are your options now?

22
00:01:19,329 --> 00:01:21,455
Um...

23
00:01:21,456 --> 00:01:25,001
up my Keppra or maybe try

24
00:01:25,002 --> 00:01:26,627
one of the newer
anti-seizure meds.

25
00:01:26,628 --> 00:01:29,463
But if that doesn't work,
I'm left with two choices--

26
00:01:29,464 --> 00:01:33,884
um, a temporal lobectomy,
which could impair my speech,

27
00:01:33,885 --> 00:01:36,345
or get a neuromodulation
device,

28
00:01:36,346 --> 00:01:38,097
which can sense
and stop the seizures

29
00:01:38,098 --> 00:01:39,932
almost immediately.

30
00:01:39,933 --> 00:01:41,767
You need to disclose this.

31
00:01:41,768 --> 00:01:43,811
I know. I have a plan.

32
00:01:43,812 --> 00:01:44,895
Hey, Robby,
Dana's looking for you.

33
00:01:44,896 --> 00:01:46,147
She's in Peds.

34
00:01:46,148 --> 00:01:47,399
Yeah, OK,
I'll be right there.

35
00:01:48,859 --> 00:01:50,067
Sounds like
you're needed in Peds,

36
00:01:50,068 --> 00:01:52,194
and I have patients to see.

37
00:01:52,195 --> 00:01:54,113
Robby, pregnant woman
with severe headache

38
00:01:54,114 --> 00:01:55,823
on her way in by ambulance.

39
00:01:55,824 --> 00:01:58,243
Find Abbot
or a night shift resident.

40
00:02:13,342 --> 00:02:15,177
Need you to turn out
your pockets.

41
00:02:21,475 --> 00:02:23,310
OK. Show me your hands.

42
00:02:51,296 --> 00:02:52,631
Come here often?

43
00:03:01,431 --> 00:03:02,932
What's going on?

44
00:03:02,933 --> 00:03:04,684
Oh, sorry--false alarm.

45
00:03:04,685 --> 00:03:06,894
We thought she spiked a fever,
but it was the wrong chart

46
00:03:06,895 --> 00:03:09,313
from our analog hell.

47
00:03:09,314 --> 00:03:11,899
You know anybody who might
consider kinship adoption?

48
00:03:11,900 --> 00:03:13,651
Doctors and nurses qualify.

49
00:03:13,652 --> 00:03:15,277
Don't look at me.

50
00:03:15,278 --> 00:03:17,405
Hey, can your staff
keep an eye on Dr. Al-Hashimi

51
00:03:17,406 --> 00:03:18,447
until she leaves?

52
00:03:18,448 --> 00:03:20,908
Why?

53
00:03:20,909 --> 00:03:23,077
Uh, because I think
she's tired,

54
00:03:23,078 --> 00:03:24,662
and I don't want her
to make any mistakes.

55
00:03:24,663 --> 00:03:26,747
Oh, great advice.
Maybe you should take it.

56
00:03:26,748 --> 00:03:27,998
Yeah.

57
00:03:27,999 --> 00:03:29,458
I'm gonna go get
some fresh air.

58
00:03:29,459 --> 00:03:31,001
Grab some for me
while you're out there.

59
00:03:31,002 --> 00:03:32,128
Your lungs wouldn't know
what to do with it.

60
00:03:32,129 --> 00:03:33,170
Screw you!

61
00:03:33,171 --> 00:03:34,756
In front of the baby? Nice.

62
00:03:37,676 --> 00:03:39,301
Yeah.

63
00:03:39,302 --> 00:03:41,178
We are the night crawlers.

64
00:03:41,179 --> 00:03:44,140
We deal with the weirdest
and the wildest because...

65
00:03:44,141 --> 00:03:46,684
all: We are the weirdest
and the wildest of them all.

66
00:03:46,685 --> 00:03:47,810
That is right, and tonight,

67
00:03:47,811 --> 00:03:49,145
they are really gonna be
crawling.

68
00:03:49,146 --> 00:03:50,521
Now go get some!

69
00:03:50,522 --> 00:03:51,481
all: Hooah!

70
00:03:55,986 --> 00:03:57,570
Sorry to wake you.

71
00:03:57,571 --> 00:03:58,989
I--I was thinking.

72
00:04:02,868 --> 00:04:04,201
Doubt PTX.

73
00:04:04,202 --> 00:04:06,454
You're supposed
to be leaving.

74
00:04:06,455 --> 00:04:07,539
I am.

75
00:04:09,833 --> 00:04:11,417
You know,
this spirit quest of yours

76
00:04:11,418 --> 00:04:13,294
has a lot of people
up in arms around here.

77
00:04:13,295 --> 00:04:14,754
Everyone's gonna be fine
without me,

78
00:04:14,755 --> 00:04:16,380
and it's hardly a spirit quest.

79
00:04:16,381 --> 00:04:18,090
Whatever it is,
it seems you've given people

80
00:04:18,091 --> 00:04:19,341
the impression
you might not be coming back.

81
00:04:19,342 --> 00:04:20,801
Well, who knows

82
00:04:20,802 --> 00:04:22,261
what the future has in store
for any of us?

83
00:04:22,262 --> 00:04:23,637
Yeah, saying shit
like that right there

84
00:04:23,638 --> 00:04:24,680
isn't helping.

85
00:04:24,681 --> 00:04:26,098
People are worried about you.

86
00:04:26,099 --> 00:04:28,017
Dr. Abbot,
the patient in South 21,

87
00:04:28,018 --> 00:04:29,477
Digby, he's missing again.

88
00:04:29,478 --> 00:04:30,853
Sounds like
a day shift problem.

89
00:04:30,854 --> 00:04:33,023
Not if he was
handed off already.

90
00:04:37,277 --> 00:04:38,903
Best I can do
under the circumstances.

91
00:04:38,904 --> 00:04:40,196
Thank you.

92
00:04:40,197 --> 00:04:41,697
Hey, don't leave
before I get back, yeah?

93
00:04:41,698 --> 00:04:43,450
Hell, I feel like
I live here now.

94
00:04:46,870 --> 00:04:48,204
Your friend fixing your bike?

95
00:04:48,205 --> 00:04:49,455
Ambulance clipped it

96
00:04:49,456 --> 00:04:51,332
while it was just
parked here today.

97
00:04:51,333 --> 00:04:53,542
Jesus Christ.

98
00:04:53,543 --> 00:04:55,086
That's a sign
if I've ever seen one.

99
00:04:56,713 --> 00:04:58,547
Yeah, here's the thing--
when people worry about you,

100
00:04:58,548 --> 00:05:00,299
it makes me think that
I should be worried about you,

101
00:05:00,300 --> 00:05:01,967
and I don't like worrying
about things.

102
00:05:01,968 --> 00:05:03,177
Ooh. Now you're a shrink?

103
00:05:03,178 --> 00:05:04,261
No, I'm trying
to be your friend.

104
00:05:04,262 --> 00:05:05,429
You got--you got Dana convinced

105
00:05:05,430 --> 00:05:07,223
that you're gonna
hurt yourself.

106
00:05:07,224 --> 00:05:08,766
- Dana's got her own issues.
- That sounds like projection.

107
00:05:08,767 --> 00:05:10,100
Are you seriously trying
to have this fucking

108
00:05:10,101 --> 00:05:11,685
conversation with me
right now, man?

109
00:05:11,686 --> 00:05:13,270
I--I'm not the one

110
00:05:13,271 --> 00:05:15,648
who spends his free time
getting shot at.

111
00:05:15,649 --> 00:05:17,233
Hooah!

112
00:05:17,234 --> 00:05:19,568
Hey, Dr. Robby,
this is Judith Lastrade--

113
00:05:19,569 --> 00:05:21,821
36 weeks pregnant
with two days of headache,

114
00:05:21,822 --> 00:05:24,323
now a 10 out of 10
with blurred vision.

115
00:05:24,324 --> 00:05:27,535
BP 174/120, heart rate 92.

116
00:05:27,536 --> 00:05:29,620
- No relief with fentanyl.
- Judith, I'm Dr. Abbot.

117
00:05:29,621 --> 00:05:31,038
Any weakness
in your arms or legs?

118
00:05:31,039 --> 00:05:32,581
No, no. Is this a stroke?

119
00:05:32,582 --> 00:05:33,958
We need to check
for everything.

120
00:05:33,959 --> 00:05:36,710
Pitting edema
with severe preeclampsia.

121
00:05:36,711 --> 00:05:38,629
Where are you doing
your prenatal care?

122
00:05:38,630 --> 00:05:39,880
Nowhere.

123
00:05:39,881 --> 00:05:41,382
It's a wild pregnancy.

124
00:05:41,383 --> 00:05:43,218
I want a free birth.

125
00:05:45,428 --> 00:05:48,848
This 81-year-old nun
presents with red, itchy eyes

126
00:05:48,849 --> 00:05:52,017
with secretions
for the past two days.

127
00:05:52,018 --> 00:05:54,520
Patient complains
of no URI symptoms,

128
00:05:54,521 --> 00:05:56,105
- no contact with any chemical...
- Hey.

129
00:05:56,106 --> 00:05:57,481
Agents,
no known exposures--

130
00:05:57,482 --> 00:05:59,024
Want half a Monster?

131
00:05:59,025 --> 00:06:00,693
Oh, no, thanks.

132
00:06:00,694 --> 00:06:02,194
I--I don't really want
to stay awake

133
00:06:02,195 --> 00:06:04,321
any longer than I have to.

134
00:06:04,322 --> 00:06:05,782
Yeah, I hear you.

135
00:06:07,325 --> 00:06:09,410
Did you find your ID badge?

136
00:06:09,411 --> 00:06:10,953
Uh, no.

137
00:06:10,954 --> 00:06:13,247
You any closer to deciding
what's next for you?

138
00:06:13,248 --> 00:06:15,165
Uh, yeah, I'm seriously
considering law school.

139
00:06:15,166 --> 00:06:16,667
What?
What are you talking about?

140
00:06:16,668 --> 00:06:18,545
You're gonna be a great doctor.

141
00:06:20,005 --> 00:06:23,299
I mean, no offense, but look
what this place does to you.

142
00:06:23,300 --> 00:06:24,967
Langdon's an addict.

143
00:06:24,968 --> 00:06:27,678
Is a person with
a substance use disorder.

144
00:06:27,679 --> 00:06:29,638
McKay was on house arrest.

145
00:06:29,639 --> 00:06:31,140
Dana's a time bomb.

146
00:06:31,141 --> 00:06:32,850
Santos is one
of the angriest people

147
00:06:32,851 --> 00:06:34,351
you are ever going to meet.

148
00:06:34,352 --> 00:06:35,853
Sarcastic, yes.
Cynical, definitely.

149
00:06:35,854 --> 00:06:37,396
I don't know
if she's, you know--

150
00:06:37,397 --> 00:06:38,732
Mel?

151
00:06:39,816 --> 00:06:42,818
Samira has no life.

152
00:06:42,819 --> 00:06:46,030
Abbot's an adrenaline junkie
who gets shot at for fun.

153
00:06:46,031 --> 00:06:48,908
Robby's got, like, PTSD
or something way fucking worse.

154
00:06:48,909 --> 00:06:50,159
OK, well, I--I mean,

155
00:06:50,160 --> 00:06:52,120
I'd hate to know
what you think about me.

156
00:06:53,788 --> 00:06:55,456
I don't know, I just--

157
00:06:55,457 --> 00:06:58,083
the more time I spend here,

158
00:06:58,084 --> 00:06:59,335
the more I realize
the importance

159
00:06:59,336 --> 00:07:01,922
of my mental health.

160
00:07:03,048 --> 00:07:04,173
Mm.

161
00:07:04,174 --> 00:07:05,466
For patients and for us.

162
00:07:05,467 --> 00:07:08,052
And this is...

163
00:07:08,053 --> 00:07:09,219
Yeah.

164
00:07:09,220 --> 00:07:10,512
Well, you know,

165
00:07:10,513 --> 00:07:13,266
maybe that's
what you should focus on.

166
00:07:14,434 --> 00:07:16,685
- What?
- Mental health.

167
00:07:16,686 --> 00:07:18,979
Clearly, you have
a passion for it, right?

168
00:07:18,980 --> 00:07:20,522
I mean, that's--that's great.

169
00:07:20,523 --> 00:07:21,607
I don't know if
I'd call it a passion.

170
00:07:21,608 --> 00:07:23,693
I would call it, like, a...

171
00:07:26,655 --> 00:07:28,198
Oh, my God.

172
00:07:30,158 --> 00:07:32,243
You might be right.

173
00:07:33,870 --> 00:07:35,496
Oh, you're a genius, Whitaker.

174
00:07:35,497 --> 00:07:36,665
Oh, OK.

175
00:07:38,333 --> 00:07:40,334
CTG is on.

176
00:07:40,335 --> 00:07:42,628
- CTG?
- Cardiotocography.

177
00:07:42,629 --> 00:07:46,048
Measures the baby's heart rate
and checks for contractions.

178
00:07:46,049 --> 00:07:47,633
Fetal heart rate 128.

179
00:07:47,634 --> 00:07:49,176
Normal range, Nazely?

180
00:07:49,177 --> 00:07:51,053
110 to 160.

181
00:07:51,054 --> 00:07:52,930
So the baby's OK?

182
00:07:52,931 --> 00:07:54,139
Right now, yes.

183
00:07:54,140 --> 00:07:55,557
128 is reassuring.

184
00:07:55,558 --> 00:07:57,768
BP's 170/119.

185
00:07:57,769 --> 00:07:59,561
6 grams of magnesium
running in.

186
00:07:59,562 --> 00:08:01,146
Your next move, Crus?

187
00:08:01,147 --> 00:08:03,774
20 of labetalol,
IV push over two minutes.

188
00:08:03,775 --> 00:08:05,317
Uh, what's happening?

189
00:08:05,318 --> 00:08:07,361
Uh, you have a condition
called preeclampsia.

190
00:08:07,362 --> 00:08:08,612
And how did it happen?

191
00:08:08,613 --> 00:08:10,864
Uh, nobody really knows, actually.

192
00:08:10,865 --> 00:08:13,200
It affects about 10%
of the pregnancies.

193
00:08:13,201 --> 00:08:14,660
High blood pressure, headaches,

194
00:08:14,661 --> 00:08:17,121
protein in the urine,
and swollen ankles.

195
00:08:17,122 --> 00:08:19,415
OK, well,
it's a wild pregnancy,

196
00:08:19,416 --> 00:08:21,625
so that means no medical care.

197
00:08:21,626 --> 00:08:23,586
Then why are you here?

198
00:08:25,130 --> 00:08:27,340
I just need to get rid
of this headache.

199
00:08:29,551 --> 00:08:32,594
Well, if we don't lower
your blood pressure

200
00:08:32,595 --> 00:08:35,514
and treat with magnesium,
there can be problems.

201
00:08:35,515 --> 00:08:36,765
Like what?

202
00:08:36,766 --> 00:08:38,392
Seizures, bleeding,

203
00:08:38,393 --> 00:08:40,477
even death,
for you and the baby.

204
00:08:40,478 --> 00:08:42,312
Oh, my God.

205
00:08:42,313 --> 00:08:44,023
Robby, your VIP's
ready to go.

206
00:08:44,024 --> 00:08:46,108
OK, I'll be right there.

207
00:08:46,109 --> 00:08:47,735
- You good?
- Yeah, I'm good.

208
00:08:47,736 --> 00:08:50,446
I got it.
With my eyes closed.

209
00:08:50,447 --> 00:08:51,698
But I won't. Maybe one eye.

210
00:08:53,116 --> 00:08:54,159
Hey--

211
00:08:57,579 --> 00:08:58,996
Hey, Becca.
How you feeling?

212
00:08:58,997 --> 00:09:01,166
<i>I'm better. Thanks.</i>

213
00:09:02,751 --> 00:09:04,126
Where are you?

214
00:09:04,127 --> 00:09:06,045
<i>I'm at Adam's house.</i>

215
00:09:06,046 --> 00:09:07,796
<i>Can I call you later?
We're watching a movie.</i>

216
00:09:07,797 --> 00:09:09,048
Oh, sure.
I just--I thought

217
00:09:09,049 --> 00:09:10,591
you were gonna see
the fireworks.

218
00:09:10,592 --> 00:09:13,177
<i>Nope, we decided
to watch "Elf" instead.</i>

219
00:09:13,178 --> 00:09:14,511
Ah.

220
00:09:14,512 --> 00:09:16,513
- Of course you did.
<i>- OK.</i>

221
00:09:16,514 --> 00:09:18,223
<i>- I'll call you tomorrow!</i>
- Tomorrow? Wait.

222
00:09:18,224 --> 00:09:20,517
Uh, are--are you
spending the night?

223
00:09:20,518 --> 00:09:22,394
<i>Um, uh, yes.</i>

224
00:09:22,395 --> 00:09:24,146
<i>His parents invited me.</i>

225
00:09:24,147 --> 00:09:25,647
They--they need
to ask me that.

226
00:09:25,648 --> 00:09:28,108
<i>Are--are you
staying here too?</i>

227
00:09:28,109 --> 00:09:32,154
No, they--they needed to ask
if it was OK if you stayed.

228
00:09:32,155 --> 00:09:33,530
<i>Why?</i>

229
00:09:33,531 --> 00:09:38,202
Be--because, uh,
it's polite.

230
00:09:38,203 --> 00:09:40,496
It's the right--
it's the right thing to do.

231
00:09:40,497 --> 00:09:43,582
Um, I need to talk to them.

232
00:09:43,583 --> 00:09:46,293
<i>Um, they're not here.
They're at a barbecue.</i>

233
00:09:46,294 --> 00:09:48,420
OK, um,
can you have them call me

234
00:09:48,421 --> 00:09:49,755
as soon as they get home?

235
00:09:49,756 --> 00:09:51,632
<i>- Yes.</i>
- Can you promise?

236
00:09:51,633 --> 00:09:53,509
<i>I promise.
OK, bye, Mel!</i>

237
00:09:53,510 --> 00:09:54,886
Bye. Have fun--

238
00:09:56,304 --> 00:09:57,888
Thanks for fixing my bike.

239
00:09:57,889 --> 00:10:00,058
Well, you keep me running,
I'll keep her going.

240
00:10:01,976 --> 00:10:05,521
You know, the Cree don't have
a word for goodbye.

241
00:10:05,522 --> 00:10:06,606
You know a lot of Cree?

242
00:10:07,607 --> 00:10:08,649
A bit.

243
00:10:08,650 --> 00:10:09,608
I got around, man.

244
00:10:09,609 --> 00:10:10,819
I don't doubt it.

245
00:10:13,446 --> 00:10:15,906
Look, I'll come back
for all this other shit...

246
00:10:15,907 --> 00:10:17,282
Great.

247
00:10:17,283 --> 00:10:18,742
If you promise to come back

248
00:10:18,743 --> 00:10:20,619
and let me take
the Bonnie for a ride.

249
00:10:20,620 --> 00:10:21,829
Uh, I don't know.

250
00:10:21,830 --> 00:10:23,205
I've seen you ride, old man.

251
00:10:23,206 --> 00:10:24,665
Fuck you.

252
00:10:24,666 --> 00:10:26,583
I mean it.

253
00:10:26,584 --> 00:10:27,752
We got a deal?

254
00:10:30,880 --> 00:10:32,715
I'll think about it.

255
00:10:45,895 --> 00:10:47,938
This looks like an ambush.

256
00:10:47,939 --> 00:10:49,606
We got a slight hiccup
in chairs.

257
00:10:49,607 --> 00:10:50,691
ICE is back?

258
00:10:50,692 --> 00:10:52,693
No, we got a dead body.

259
00:10:52,694 --> 00:10:54,319
- Somebody died out there?
- Yeah.

260
00:10:54,320 --> 00:10:56,113
Poor devil checked in
at 5:00 this morning.

261
00:10:56,114 --> 00:10:57,614
He was a DNR.

262
00:10:57,615 --> 00:10:58,782
- What was his chief complaint?
- Hemorrhoids

263
00:10:58,783 --> 00:11:00,325
- and constipation.
- No shit.

264
00:11:00,326 --> 00:11:02,661
Hence the constipation.

265
00:11:02,662 --> 00:11:04,413
Throw me a slow one,
I'm gonna hit it.

266
00:11:04,414 --> 00:11:06,081
Tell the night shift.
I'm saying that's when he died.

267
00:11:06,082 --> 00:11:07,332
We all in agreement on that?

268
00:11:07,333 --> 00:11:08,709
To the grave.

269
00:11:08,710 --> 00:11:10,460
Just like poor Jasper.

270
00:11:10,461 --> 00:11:11,962
You're on fire.

271
00:11:11,963 --> 00:11:13,381
Just getting my second wind.

272
00:11:14,716 --> 00:11:15,966
How's the headache?

273
00:11:15,967 --> 00:11:17,301
Still a 10.

274
00:11:17,302 --> 00:11:18,802
More fentanyl?

275
00:11:18,803 --> 00:11:21,221
- Yep.
- BP's good. Another 50.

276
00:11:21,222 --> 00:11:22,681
Hey, Abbot.

277
00:11:22,682 --> 00:11:24,641
Attending and resident
are stuck in the OR.

278
00:11:24,642 --> 00:11:26,476
Oh, you're
the next best thing.

279
00:11:26,477 --> 00:11:27,853
Better, some would say.

280
00:11:27,854 --> 00:11:29,188
Mm.

281
00:11:29,189 --> 00:11:30,731
- What do you got?
- This is Judith.

282
00:11:30,732 --> 00:11:33,192
G1, P0 with no prenatal care.

283
00:11:33,193 --> 00:11:35,277
Preeclampsia
with severe hypertension.

284
00:11:35,278 --> 00:11:37,738
Hi, Judith.
Nurse Garvin from OB.

285
00:11:37,739 --> 00:11:39,156
Some jelly on the belly.

286
00:11:39,157 --> 00:11:40,741
Gonna take a quick look
with ultrasound.

287
00:11:40,742 --> 00:11:42,659
No, no, no.
Ultrasound can harm the baby.

288
00:11:42,660 --> 00:11:44,661
- Not true.
- Not doing the ultrasound

289
00:11:44,662 --> 00:11:46,706
could end up harming you
and the baby.

290
00:11:48,666 --> 00:11:51,752
OK.
Just do it as fast as you can.

291
00:11:51,753 --> 00:11:54,130
Why no prenatal care, Judith?

292
00:11:55,256 --> 00:11:57,674
I wanted a free birth--

293
00:11:57,675 --> 00:11:59,843
no doctors, no hospital,
no medicine.

294
00:11:59,844 --> 00:12:02,679
Mm. You have a midwife?

295
00:12:02,680 --> 00:12:03,764
A birth doula?

296
00:12:03,765 --> 00:12:06,183
No, I don't need one.

297
00:12:06,184 --> 00:12:07,476
Women have been having
children on their own

298
00:12:07,477 --> 00:12:08,727
for thousands of years.

299
00:12:08,728 --> 00:12:10,270
Yeah, with
an infant mortality rate

300
00:12:10,271 --> 00:12:13,148
of 30% for most of those
thousands of years.

301
00:12:13,149 --> 00:12:15,442
- Femur length 7 centimeters.
- 37 weeks.

302
00:12:15,443 --> 00:12:17,402
They'll probably induce.

303
00:12:17,403 --> 00:12:19,321
What? No.

304
00:12:19,322 --> 00:12:20,697
No, no, no, no. Absolutely not.

305
00:12:20,698 --> 00:12:22,241
At 37 weeks,

306
00:12:22,242 --> 00:12:24,451
the cure for preeclampsia
is to deliver the baby.

307
00:12:24,452 --> 00:12:26,245
We need to get you upstairs
so the OB doctors

308
00:12:26,246 --> 00:12:28,997
can induce labor
to save you and your baby.

309
00:12:28,998 --> 00:12:31,417
No. No, no, no, no. Mm-mm.

310
00:12:33,795 --> 00:12:35,504
Yep, that's
definitely Jasper.

311
00:12:35,505 --> 00:12:36,797
He was alive and kicking

312
00:12:36,798 --> 00:12:38,173
when my shift ended
this morning.

313
00:12:38,174 --> 00:12:39,549
This is definitely
a day shift patient.

314
00:12:39,550 --> 00:12:40,884
Now he's not a patient.

315
00:12:40,885 --> 00:12:42,345
He's a DB that
we gotta deal with.

316
00:12:44,889 --> 00:12:46,181
Is this dude dead?

317
00:12:46,182 --> 00:12:47,683
both: Nope.

318
00:12:47,684 --> 00:12:49,518
All right, Mr. Reed,
time to take you back

319
00:12:49,519 --> 00:12:50,978
and get you checked out, OK?

320
00:12:50,979 --> 00:12:52,396
- He sure looks dead.
- Are you a doctor?

321
00:12:52,397 --> 00:12:54,731
- No, but he--
- Has hypernarcolepsy.

322
00:12:54,732 --> 00:12:56,483
- It's no joke.
- Mm-hmm.

323
00:12:56,484 --> 00:12:57,652
Excuse me.

324
00:12:58,736 --> 00:13:00,696
Oh, sometimes I hate nights.

325
00:13:00,697 --> 00:13:01,864
- Yep.
- Oof.

326
00:13:12,834 --> 00:13:14,209
Wow.

327
00:13:14,210 --> 00:13:17,421
Crazy how muggy
it still is out here.

328
00:13:17,422 --> 00:13:20,132
You, uh--you seen Robby?

329
00:13:20,133 --> 00:13:22,301
Uh, not for a bit.

330
00:13:22,302 --> 00:13:23,635
You catch up on your charts

331
00:13:23,636 --> 00:13:25,137
from the beginning
of the shift?

332
00:13:25,138 --> 00:13:26,388
Yeah.

333
00:13:26,389 --> 00:13:27,472
What are you still
doing here?

334
00:13:27,473 --> 00:13:29,266
Uh, just gonna...

335
00:13:29,267 --> 00:13:31,685
You staying
for the fireworks?

336
00:13:31,686 --> 00:13:33,061
Yeah.

337
00:13:33,062 --> 00:13:34,479
I was supposed to see them
with Becca,

338
00:13:34,480 --> 00:13:38,483
but she is
at her boyfriend Adam's

339
00:13:38,484 --> 00:13:40,320
family's house instead.

340
00:13:44,657 --> 00:13:50,871
Your sister seems like
she's, uh, pretty put-together.

341
00:13:50,872 --> 00:13:52,164
Yeah.

342
00:13:52,165 --> 00:13:54,876
Uh, a lot more than I realized.

343
00:13:56,794 --> 00:13:58,212
How was your day?

344
00:14:00,089 --> 00:14:02,591
I've had better.

345
00:14:02,592 --> 00:14:03,634
You?

346
00:14:06,596 --> 00:14:09,014
Yeah.

347
00:14:09,015 --> 00:14:12,309
But then again,
I've had a lot worse.

348
00:14:12,310 --> 00:14:14,853
Hell, I did a closed cervical
reduction, like, an hour ago.

349
00:14:14,854 --> 00:14:17,065
Oh, I heard.
That must have been so intense.

350
00:14:18,775 --> 00:14:20,984
My hands are still shaking.

351
00:14:20,985 --> 00:14:23,028
Hey, um, do you think
you could teach me

352
00:14:23,029 --> 00:14:25,155
how to do that sometime?

353
00:14:25,156 --> 00:14:26,615
Uh, yeah.

354
00:14:26,616 --> 00:14:27,824
- Yeah?
- Yeah, sure. I mean,

355
00:14:27,825 --> 00:14:29,409
I hope you never
have to use it.

356
00:14:29,410 --> 00:14:31,370
I could have paralyzed
that guy.

357
00:14:31,371 --> 00:14:34,081
Yeah, but you didn't.

358
00:14:34,082 --> 00:14:37,376
No, I didn't.

359
00:14:37,377 --> 00:14:39,795
Thank you...

360
00:14:39,796 --> 00:14:41,922
by the way, for...

361
00:14:41,923 --> 00:14:44,633
talking me down earlier.

362
00:14:44,634 --> 00:14:46,469
I'm sorry I snapped.

363
00:14:48,054 --> 00:14:49,347
It's OK.

364
00:14:57,522 --> 00:15:00,190
Dr. Mohan, you ever heard
of kinship fostering?

365
00:15:00,191 --> 00:15:01,942
It's where a nurse
or doctor can

366
00:15:01,943 --> 00:15:03,443
- become an emergency foster--
- Oh, no.

367
00:15:03,444 --> 00:15:04,945
I don't need any kids.

368
00:15:04,946 --> 00:15:07,114
I need to find a job first.

369
00:15:07,115 --> 00:15:09,533
Candice O'Grady is
an 82-year-old female

370
00:15:09,534 --> 00:15:12,077
brought in by her son
for intractable vomiting.

371
00:15:12,078 --> 00:15:14,997
No fever, no chills,
no abdominal pain, no rash.

372
00:15:16,124 --> 00:15:18,125
Beep.

373
00:15:18,126 --> 00:15:21,503
Oh, I've already got one
I can barely keep up with.

374
00:15:21,504 --> 00:15:23,422
What about Sleeping Beauty
over here?

375
00:15:23,423 --> 00:15:25,465
She's already babysitting
Whitaker.

376
00:15:25,466 --> 00:15:27,509
Well, if you know anyone
who'd like to help us out

377
00:15:27,510 --> 00:15:29,469
with Baby Jane Doe,
have them call the main desk.

378
00:15:29,470 --> 00:15:31,096
Sure thing.

379
00:15:31,097 --> 00:15:34,183
I'd take her myself,
but Benji'd kill me.

380
00:15:35,643 --> 00:15:37,436
BP's 164/114.

381
00:15:37,437 --> 00:15:38,812
Another 40 of labetalol.

382
00:15:38,813 --> 00:15:39,938
Mag bolus is in.

383
00:15:39,939 --> 00:15:41,606
Now infusing 2 grams an hour.

384
00:15:41,607 --> 00:15:42,858
Labs are coming back.

385
00:15:42,859 --> 00:15:45,152
Hemoglobin 7.5, platelets 40.

386
00:15:45,153 --> 00:15:47,154
LFTs are sky high.

387
00:15:47,155 --> 00:15:48,905
- HELLP syndrome.
- Hemolytic anemia,

388
00:15:48,906 --> 00:15:51,283
elevated liver enzymes,
and low platelets.

389
00:15:51,284 --> 00:15:52,659
They're cleaning a room.

390
00:15:52,660 --> 00:15:54,578
We can bring her up
in ten minutes.

391
00:15:54,579 --> 00:15:55,746
How you doing, Judith?

392
00:15:57,832 --> 00:15:59,917
I--I--

393
00:16:00,835 --> 00:16:02,043
Oh, she's seizing.

394
00:16:02,044 --> 00:16:03,712
Oh, shit.

395
00:16:03,713 --> 00:16:06,256
10 of IV diazepam.
Have another 10 ready.

396
00:16:06,257 --> 00:16:08,258
With all the movement,
we can't get a fetal heartbeat.

397
00:16:08,259 --> 00:16:10,552
Putting on 15 liters by mask.
Should we intubate?

398
00:16:10,553 --> 00:16:12,554
Hold intubation.
Let's try to break this.

399
00:16:12,555 --> 00:16:14,473
We don't want to mask seizures
with paralysis

400
00:16:14,474 --> 00:16:16,057
unless we have to.

401
00:16:16,058 --> 00:16:17,518
OK, um...

402
00:16:20,062 --> 00:16:21,855
Crus, CTG isn't reading.

403
00:16:21,856 --> 00:16:23,315
- Check with ultrasound.
- On it.

404
00:16:23,316 --> 00:16:24,900
Nazely, what's the diagnosis?

405
00:16:24,901 --> 00:16:27,862
Um, with the seizure,
now it's eclampsia.

406
00:16:29,155 --> 00:16:31,198
- Fetal heart rate is about 90.
- Way too low.

407
00:16:31,199 --> 00:16:32,449
Mom's sats are going down.

408
00:16:32,450 --> 00:16:33,909
Time to tube her?

409
00:16:33,910 --> 00:16:35,577
Set up for it, but wait.

410
00:16:35,578 --> 00:16:36,912
Another 10 of diazepam.

411
00:16:36,913 --> 00:16:39,332
Push 4 grams of Keppra.

412
00:16:42,168 --> 00:16:43,668
History of hypertension

413
00:16:43,669 --> 00:16:45,003
presents to the emergency
department

414
00:16:45,004 --> 00:16:47,339
with a chief complaint
of dizziness

415
00:16:47,340 --> 00:16:49,549
after inadvertently
ingesting 80 milligrams--

416
00:16:49,550 --> 00:16:50,842
Hey, how are you guys
making out?

417
00:16:50,843 --> 00:16:51,927
Yeah, we're getting there.

418
00:16:51,928 --> 00:16:53,678
Have you seen Dr. Al-Hashimi?

419
00:16:53,679 --> 00:16:55,473
- No.
- Can I talk to you for a sec?

420
00:17:01,062 --> 00:17:02,395
So I just wanted
to let you know that I've been

421
00:17:02,396 --> 00:17:03,647
checking out some
of your online posts--

422
00:17:03,648 --> 00:17:04,856
Look, I was just
trying to help

423
00:17:04,857 --> 00:17:06,441
get some health messages
out there,

424
00:17:06,442 --> 00:17:07,984
- especially for young people.
- I think they're great.

425
00:17:07,985 --> 00:17:09,986
Really good.

426
00:17:09,987 --> 00:17:11,988
- You do?
- Yeah.

427
00:17:11,989 --> 00:17:14,241
Yeah, um, keep it up.

428
00:17:14,242 --> 00:17:15,659
OK.

429
00:17:15,660 --> 00:17:17,994
As long as you follow
the HIPAA laws.

430
00:17:17,995 --> 00:17:19,412
I do.

431
00:17:19,413 --> 00:17:21,248
And wait until
you're done charting.

432
00:17:21,249 --> 00:17:22,250
Sure.

433
00:17:24,794 --> 00:17:29,130
Actually, Dr. Robby--sorry,
um, can I ask you a question?

434
00:17:29,131 --> 00:17:30,340
Shoot.

435
00:17:30,341 --> 00:17:31,841
Um, I--I may be

436
00:17:31,842 --> 00:17:34,554
considering
emergency psychiatry.

437
00:17:35,846 --> 00:17:38,098
Very cool.

438
00:17:38,099 --> 00:17:39,767
Think I could do it?

439
00:17:42,019 --> 00:17:43,562
I think that you could do

440
00:17:43,563 --> 00:17:46,065
anything that you put
your mind to, Victoria.

441
00:17:50,236 --> 00:17:51,653
OK.

442
00:17:51,654 --> 00:17:53,281
Pulse ox is 88.

443
00:17:54,574 --> 00:17:56,616
Dr. Abbot?

444
00:17:56,617 --> 00:17:58,785
- Intubate?
- Let's do it.

445
00:17:58,786 --> 00:18:02,122
Nazely, what do you suggest
for rapid sequence induction?

446
00:18:02,123 --> 00:18:03,331
Etomidate and roc.

447
00:18:03,332 --> 00:18:04,499
Mm, not quite.

448
00:18:04,500 --> 00:18:05,625
120 of propofol,

449
00:18:05,626 --> 00:18:06,626
60 of succinylcholine.

450
00:18:06,627 --> 00:18:08,086
Why is that, Crus?

451
00:18:08,087 --> 00:18:09,796
Propofol
for the anti-seizure effect,

452
00:18:09,797 --> 00:18:11,423
sux to avoid
prolonged paralysis

453
00:18:11,424 --> 00:18:13,508
- so we can check her neuro exam.
- Exactly.

454
00:18:13,509 --> 00:18:14,843
Pushing the propofol.

455
00:18:14,844 --> 00:18:16,344
Once she's flat
for intubation,

456
00:18:16,345 --> 00:18:17,929
we need to displace
the uterus to the left.

457
00:18:17,930 --> 00:18:19,556
Nazely, that's you.
Big hug, both arms.

458
00:18:19,557 --> 00:18:21,891
- Get the baby off the vena cava.
- Sux is on board.

459
00:18:21,892 --> 00:18:24,644
But after she's paralyzed,
the seizing stops, right?

460
00:18:24,645 --> 00:18:26,146
It might look like that,

461
00:18:26,147 --> 00:18:28,189
but an ongoing seizure
will still fry the brain.

462
00:18:28,190 --> 00:18:30,025
We monitor with EEG.

463
00:18:30,026 --> 00:18:31,819
- Is there time for that?
- Wait and see.

464
00:18:33,029 --> 00:18:34,321
Paralytics kicked in.

465
00:18:34,322 --> 00:18:35,823
Let's go.
Roll her to her back.

466
00:18:36,866 --> 00:18:38,575
Intubate, then EEG

467
00:18:38,576 --> 00:18:41,119
to see if her brain is
still seizing.

468
00:18:41,120 --> 00:18:42,662
I need first pass success.

469
00:18:42,663 --> 00:18:43,831
You and me both.

470
00:18:52,757 --> 00:18:54,174
Have you seen Dr. Al-Hashimi?

471
00:18:54,175 --> 00:18:55,383
No.

472
00:18:55,384 --> 00:18:57,761
Have you seen Dr. Al-Hashimi?

473
00:18:57,762 --> 00:18:59,554
Al-Hashimi?

474
00:18:59,555 --> 00:19:02,140
With how this day's going,
she probably quit.

475
00:19:02,141 --> 00:19:05,393
Last I saw her, she was
in Peds with Baby Jane Doe.

476
00:19:05,394 --> 00:19:07,812
Nope, I was just in there.

477
00:19:07,813 --> 00:19:08,813
Want me to page her?

478
00:19:08,814 --> 00:19:10,607
Uh, no, that's OK.

479
00:19:10,608 --> 00:19:11,901
I will find her.

480
00:19:16,530 --> 00:19:17,740
Hello.

481
00:19:20,576 --> 00:19:22,994
Hey, how did our people do
at the deposition?

482
00:19:22,995 --> 00:19:25,538
Oh, well,
Dr. Ellis is a pit bull.

483
00:19:25,539 --> 00:19:27,624
Dr. King is a petunia.

484
00:19:27,625 --> 00:19:28,958
They were pretty brutal
with her.

485
00:19:28,959 --> 00:19:30,835
- She's sensitive.
- Very.

486
00:19:30,836 --> 00:19:32,420
And I'm afraid it isn't over.

487
00:19:32,421 --> 00:19:33,588
They want to call her back.

488
00:19:33,589 --> 00:19:35,423
Oh, that's unfortunate.

489
00:19:35,424 --> 00:19:36,675
Maybe I should go with you

490
00:19:36,676 --> 00:19:38,343
to break that news to her, actually.

491
00:19:38,344 --> 00:19:40,178
- Misery loves company.
- Um, hey, while I have you,

492
00:19:40,179 --> 00:19:42,931
can I pose a hypothetical
to you?

493
00:19:42,932 --> 00:19:44,933
If a doctor suspects
another physician

494
00:19:44,934 --> 00:19:47,227
of having a medical condition
that could negatively

495
00:19:47,228 --> 00:19:49,354
affect the way they
would treat a patient,

496
00:19:49,355 --> 00:19:51,064
where would
disclosing that fall

497
00:19:51,065 --> 00:19:52,983
on the HIPAA violation scale?

498
00:19:54,068 --> 00:19:55,986
First, do no harm.

499
00:19:58,489 --> 00:20:00,908
Dr. King, do you have a second?

500
00:20:03,536 --> 00:20:06,247
Mm...

501
00:20:08,124 --> 00:20:10,166
Good lung sliding
bilaterally.

502
00:20:10,167 --> 00:20:12,169
Fetal heart rate
borderline at 98.

503
00:20:13,713 --> 00:20:15,880
Roll her to the left again.
That can help.

504
00:20:15,881 --> 00:20:18,050
One, two, three.

505
00:20:19,051 --> 00:20:22,512
OK, all set here.

506
00:20:22,513 --> 00:20:24,013
EEG monitor's good to go.

507
00:20:24,014 --> 00:20:25,807
That was fast.

508
00:20:25,808 --> 00:20:27,267
Still seizing
while paralyzed.

509
00:20:27,268 --> 00:20:29,811
It's nonconvulsive status.

510
00:20:29,812 --> 00:20:31,187
What's she had so far?

511
00:20:31,188 --> 00:20:32,856
30 of diazepam,
a full load of mag,

512
00:20:32,857 --> 00:20:34,065
Keppra, and propofol.

513
00:20:34,066 --> 00:20:35,442
Damn. What's your next step?

514
00:20:35,443 --> 00:20:36,651
Any ideas?

515
00:20:36,652 --> 00:20:38,903
Hmm? Nazely?

516
00:20:38,904 --> 00:20:40,822
Dilantin? Valproate?

517
00:20:40,823 --> 00:20:42,157
Mm, infusion is too long.

518
00:20:42,158 --> 00:20:43,700
So is onset of action.

519
00:20:43,701 --> 00:20:45,160
Push 100 of ketamine.

520
00:20:45,161 --> 00:20:47,412
That's had results
with refractory status.

521
00:20:47,413 --> 00:20:49,706
She also has HELLP syndrome--
hemoglobin only 7,

522
00:20:49,707 --> 00:20:52,625
- platelets down to 30.
- Two units whole blood?

523
00:20:52,626 --> 00:20:55,044
O-neg is going up on
the rapid infuser as we speak.

524
00:20:55,045 --> 00:20:57,130
Uh, put the AP pads on,
just in case.

525
00:20:57,131 --> 00:20:59,924
And 10 of Decadron IV push
for the inflammatory storm.

526
00:20:59,925 --> 00:21:02,051
- Fetal heart rate up to 104.
- Hmm.

527
00:21:02,052 --> 00:21:03,386
- Little better.
- Yeah.

528
00:21:03,387 --> 00:21:05,764
She should be upstairs with OB.

529
00:21:05,765 --> 00:21:09,517
She will be
after we break this seizure.

530
00:21:09,518 --> 00:21:12,729
There was a delay
in history-taking

531
00:21:12,730 --> 00:21:15,857
due to a malfunctioning
VRI interpretation device.

532
00:21:15,858 --> 00:21:18,443
During this time,
there was a normal CBC

533
00:21:18,444 --> 00:21:20,111
and comprehensive
metabolic panel

534
00:21:20,112 --> 00:21:21,781
that came back from the lab.

535
00:21:23,282 --> 00:21:25,200
What's wrong with you,
Malfeasance?

536
00:21:25,201 --> 00:21:28,203
I have to do
another deposition.

537
00:21:28,204 --> 00:21:30,163
Oh, that sucks.

538
00:21:30,164 --> 00:21:31,999
You must have really messed up.

539
00:21:33,167 --> 00:21:34,876
Dude, I'm joking.

540
00:21:34,877 --> 00:21:35,960
You gotta lighten up.

541
00:21:35,961 --> 00:21:37,588
It's all just bullshit.

542
00:21:40,174 --> 00:21:41,549
God, you know what?
Fuck all this.

543
00:21:41,550 --> 00:21:42,885
Do you want to go get a drink?

544
00:21:44,053 --> 00:21:45,094
Me?

545
00:21:45,095 --> 00:21:46,763
Yes, you.

546
00:21:46,764 --> 00:21:49,098
You--you do go out, don't you?

547
00:21:49,099 --> 00:21:51,309
Well, I'm usually with Becca.

548
00:21:51,310 --> 00:21:52,602
Well, bring her along.

549
00:21:52,603 --> 00:21:53,937
Can she drive?

550
00:21:53,938 --> 00:21:56,148
No, and she's
with her boyfriend.

551
00:21:57,191 --> 00:21:58,609
OK, Becca.

552
00:22:00,319 --> 00:22:02,196
So it's just you and me.

553
00:22:04,406 --> 00:22:06,825
Do you like karaoke?

554
00:22:06,826 --> 00:22:08,701
You do karaoke?

555
00:22:08,702 --> 00:22:13,081
Well, what I do is more like
primal scream therapy.

556
00:22:13,082 --> 00:22:14,791
There's nothing like
getting wasted

557
00:22:14,792 --> 00:22:16,292
and just absolutely wailing

558
00:22:16,293 --> 00:22:19,087
to shake off a shit show
like today.

559
00:22:19,088 --> 00:22:20,881
I could use a fun night.

560
00:22:22,341 --> 00:22:24,217
You and me both, sister.

561
00:22:24,218 --> 00:22:25,969
There's been no improvement.

562
00:22:25,970 --> 00:22:27,554
Still seizing on the EEG.

563
00:22:27,555 --> 00:22:29,264
- Neurology has been called.
- OK. Got it.

564
00:22:29,265 --> 00:22:31,224
OB says send her up.
They have an OR ready.

565
00:22:31,225 --> 00:22:32,684
About time.

566
00:22:32,685 --> 00:22:34,394
Baby's been bradying down
a bit more.

567
00:22:34,395 --> 00:22:35,937
This one looks like
it took a turn for the worse.

568
00:22:35,938 --> 00:22:37,772
Eclampsia,
refractory seizures,

569
00:22:37,773 --> 00:22:40,066
HELLP syndrome with anemia
and thrombocytopenia.

570
00:22:40,067 --> 00:22:42,068
Yeah,
about as bad as it gets.

571
00:22:42,069 --> 00:22:43,987
V-fib!

572
00:22:43,988 --> 00:22:46,030
Chest compressions, Nazely.

573
00:22:46,031 --> 00:22:48,783
Charge to 200.

574
00:22:48,784 --> 00:22:50,243
Prep the belly.

575
00:22:50,244 --> 00:22:51,578
Get a baby warmer.

576
00:22:51,579 --> 00:22:53,246
Call the NICU. Start a timer.

577
00:22:53,247 --> 00:22:55,081
Charged.

578
00:22:55,082 --> 00:22:56,250
Clear.

579
00:22:58,168 --> 00:22:59,502
Continue compressions.

580
00:22:59,503 --> 00:23:01,921
We'll check a rhythm
in a minute.

581
00:23:01,922 --> 00:23:03,214
Gown up.

582
00:23:03,215 --> 00:23:04,549
Robby, it's you and me.

583
00:23:04,550 --> 00:23:06,551
Nazely,
what's the four-minute rule?

584
00:23:06,552 --> 00:23:08,803
Uh, not sure.

585
00:23:08,804 --> 00:23:10,597
Pregnant patient
with a viable fetus,

586
00:23:10,598 --> 00:23:12,223
you have four minutes
after cardiac arrest

587
00:23:12,224 --> 00:23:14,517
- to save the baby.
- And the mom.

588
00:23:14,518 --> 00:23:16,811
We don't call it a postmortem
C-section anymore.

589
00:23:16,812 --> 00:23:18,062
It's a resuscitative
hysterotomy

590
00:23:18,063 --> 00:23:19,564
to try to save them both.

591
00:23:19,565 --> 00:23:20,857
But she doesn't want
any medical intervention.

592
00:23:20,858 --> 00:23:22,275
That doesn't matter.

593
00:23:22,276 --> 00:23:23,776
Mom and baby are both dead
if we do nothing.

594
00:23:23,777 --> 00:23:25,570
OK, charge to 200.

595
00:23:25,571 --> 00:23:27,573
One more rhythm check and then
Abbot and I are gonna cut.

596
00:23:28,908 --> 00:23:31,492
Ellis, you and Crus
on Mom resuscitation.

597
00:23:31,493 --> 00:23:32,952
Shen, you and Nazely
take the baby.

598
00:23:32,953 --> 00:23:34,371
OK, hold compressions.

599
00:23:36,123 --> 00:23:37,707
Still V-fib.

600
00:23:37,708 --> 00:23:38,834
Clear.

601
00:23:40,169 --> 00:23:41,711
No change.
Resume compression, amp of epi.

602
00:23:41,712 --> 00:23:42,795
OK, showtime.

603
00:23:42,796 --> 00:23:44,464
We need to get this baby out
right now.

604
00:23:44,465 --> 00:23:45,507
OK, take a break.

605
00:23:48,135 --> 00:23:51,638
OK, 10 blade. Good.

606
00:23:51,639 --> 00:23:53,848
First incision is
from the xiphoid

607
00:23:53,849 --> 00:23:55,600
to the pubic symphysis

608
00:23:55,601 --> 00:23:58,561
through the skin
to the linea alba.

609
00:23:58,562 --> 00:24:00,730
Units three and four
on the infuser.

610
00:24:00,731 --> 00:24:03,566
Second incision goes
through the peritoneum,

611
00:24:03,567 --> 00:24:05,360
exposing the uterus.

612
00:24:05,361 --> 00:24:07,070
Where do you need me?

613
00:24:07,071 --> 00:24:09,322
You're with the baby.
Nazely's got the bag mask.

614
00:24:09,323 --> 00:24:11,532
You're on suction.
Stand by for intubation.

615
00:24:11,533 --> 00:24:13,034
Bladder retractors.

616
00:24:13,035 --> 00:24:14,702
Neonatal monitor
and pulse ox ready to go.

617
00:24:14,703 --> 00:24:17,121
Ellis, gentle traction.

618
00:24:17,122 --> 00:24:19,207
OK, making a small
vertical incision

619
00:24:19,208 --> 00:24:22,835
through the lower uterus
so as not to cut the baby.

620
00:24:22,836 --> 00:24:24,629
Mm-hmm.

621
00:24:24,630 --> 00:24:26,172
- Got it?
- Yep, I got it.

622
00:24:26,173 --> 00:24:27,590
- OK.
- OK.

623
00:24:27,591 --> 00:24:30,678
Using scissors
to extend superiorly.

624
00:24:32,221 --> 00:24:34,305
Ellis, hand retract
the uterus with me.

625
00:24:34,306 --> 00:24:36,141
Amniotic fluid looks good.

626
00:24:37,851 --> 00:24:39,560
Give me some fundal pressure.

627
00:24:39,561 --> 00:24:40,938
Breech position.

628
00:24:43,399 --> 00:24:46,567
OK, baby's out.

629
00:24:46,568 --> 00:24:48,320
- It's a girl.
- All right.

630
00:24:50,072 --> 00:24:53,074
Milking the cord.

631
00:24:53,075 --> 00:24:55,576
Clamping.

632
00:24:55,577 --> 00:24:57,578
Cutting.

633
00:24:57,579 --> 00:24:59,205
OK, blue and flaccid.
Coming to you, Shen.

634
00:24:59,206 --> 00:25:00,331
- You ready?
- Yeah, you got her.

635
00:25:00,332 --> 00:25:02,375
I got it, yep.

636
00:25:02,376 --> 00:25:03,669
OK.

637
00:25:07,381 --> 00:25:09,799
Poor tone, no movement.

638
00:25:09,800 --> 00:25:12,468
Keep the blow-by closer.

639
00:25:12,469 --> 00:25:13,886
She's really blue.

640
00:25:13,887 --> 00:25:16,723
Some blue is normal,
but not this much.

641
00:25:16,724 --> 00:25:18,641
- Do we need to intubate?
- Not yet, no.

642
00:25:18,642 --> 00:25:21,394
They usually pink up
with stimulation and blow-by.

643
00:25:21,395 --> 00:25:23,187
OK, removing the placenta.

644
00:25:23,188 --> 00:25:25,482
Sweeping to the left,
trying to get it in one piece.

645
00:25:27,401 --> 00:25:28,693
- Looks intact.
- Yeah.

646
00:25:28,694 --> 00:25:30,820
Nicely done.

647
00:25:30,821 --> 00:25:32,822
10 of IV Pitocin
to contract the uterus.

648
00:25:32,823 --> 00:25:35,033
And lots of massage.

649
00:25:35,034 --> 00:25:36,659
Heart rate 76.

650
00:25:36,660 --> 00:25:38,286
Less than 100 means
we need to bag.

651
00:25:38,287 --> 00:25:39,454
Suction first.

652
00:25:39,455 --> 00:25:40,539
OK.

653
00:25:42,583 --> 00:25:44,000
Hey, Jord, charge to 200.

654
00:25:44,001 --> 00:25:46,878
Stand by for the next
rhythm check.

655
00:25:46,879 --> 00:25:48,588
She grimaced. Good sign.

656
00:25:48,589 --> 00:25:49,630
Bagging.

657
00:25:49,631 --> 00:25:51,632
Pulse ox 45%.

658
00:25:51,633 --> 00:25:53,259
Oh, I've never seen it
that low.

659
00:25:53,260 --> 00:25:55,053
It's not as bad as it sounds.

660
00:25:55,054 --> 00:25:57,096
I'm more worried
about the heart rate.

661
00:25:57,097 --> 00:25:59,265
McKay, get ready with an IO
in case we need epi.

662
00:25:59,266 --> 00:26:00,601
OK.

663
00:26:02,519 --> 00:26:05,021
Rhythm check.
Hold compressions.

664
00:26:05,022 --> 00:26:06,105
Still V-fib.

665
00:26:06,106 --> 00:26:07,524
- OK, shock it.
- Clear.

666
00:26:08,609 --> 00:26:10,109
Resume compressions.

667
00:26:10,110 --> 00:26:11,611
Shen, how's she doing
over there?

668
00:26:11,612 --> 00:26:12,904
Heart rate's up to 104.

669
00:26:12,905 --> 00:26:14,155
Uh, at one minute,

670
00:26:14,156 --> 00:26:16,491
she's 0 for color,
2 for heart rate,

671
00:26:16,492 --> 00:26:17,825
1 for reflex, tone, breathing.

672
00:26:17,826 --> 00:26:19,452
APGAR of 5.

673
00:26:19,453 --> 00:26:21,370
5 out of 10. Not great.

674
00:26:21,371 --> 00:26:23,081
Pulse ox 58%.

675
00:26:23,082 --> 00:26:24,999
- Intubation?
- Uh, not yet.

676
00:26:25,000 --> 00:26:27,085
O2 sat in the 60s is normal
at one minute.

677
00:26:27,086 --> 00:26:29,962
Her heart rate and pulse ox
are trending higher.

678
00:26:29,963 --> 00:26:31,380
Let's keep doing
what we're doing.

679
00:26:31,381 --> 00:26:32,924
A little tincture of time.

680
00:26:32,925 --> 00:26:34,592
Hold compressions.

681
00:26:34,593 --> 00:26:36,677
Looks like sinus.

682
00:26:36,678 --> 00:26:38,346
Can't feel a carotid.

683
00:26:38,347 --> 00:26:39,722
No.

684
00:26:39,723 --> 00:26:41,724
Heart's barely pumping.
It's PEA.

685
00:26:41,725 --> 00:26:43,017
Back on compressions.

686
00:26:43,018 --> 00:26:44,519
Transfuse two more units.

687
00:26:44,520 --> 00:26:45,937
She needs more red cells
and platelets.

688
00:26:45,938 --> 00:26:47,647
Ongoing blood loss
from the uterus.

689
00:26:47,648 --> 00:26:49,149
Give me all the lap pads
we got, please.

690
00:26:56,657 --> 00:26:57,990
Yeah.

691
00:26:57,991 --> 00:26:59,075
OK, yeah, thanks.

692
00:26:59,076 --> 00:27:00,535
I appreciate it, honey.

693
00:27:00,536 --> 00:27:02,453
Oh, gotta go.

694
00:27:02,454 --> 00:27:03,788
Whoa, whoa, whoa!

695
00:27:03,789 --> 00:27:04,789
Hold up.

696
00:27:04,790 --> 00:27:06,290
Is there a problem here?

697
00:27:06,291 --> 00:27:08,376
Yeah, you two aren't leaving
empty-handed.

698
00:27:08,377 --> 00:27:09,378
What?

699
00:27:10,587 --> 00:27:12,131
One of you follow me.

700
00:27:13,841 --> 00:27:15,675
Rape kits are supposed
to be picked up

701
00:27:15,676 --> 00:27:18,594
within 72 hours
of collecting 'em.

702
00:27:18,595 --> 00:27:21,347
This one's been here
for over two weeks.

703
00:27:21,348 --> 00:27:23,057
That's not on us.

704
00:27:23,058 --> 00:27:24,642
Well, it's on somebody.

705
00:27:24,643 --> 00:27:26,144
It's not bad enough
these poor women

706
00:27:26,145 --> 00:27:27,728
go through an assault,
plus the indignity

707
00:27:27,729 --> 00:27:29,397
of the whole
collection process,

708
00:27:29,398 --> 00:27:31,149
but nobody from
the police department

709
00:27:31,150 --> 00:27:33,734
even has the human decency
to come get these things?

710
00:27:33,735 --> 00:27:34,861
Like nobody there
gives a flying fuck?

711
00:27:34,862 --> 00:27:36,445
OK, we got it.

712
00:27:36,446 --> 00:27:38,406
We'll see that these get
put into evidence properly.

713
00:27:38,407 --> 00:27:39,575
Thank you.

714
00:27:41,743 --> 00:27:42,911
How hard was that?

715
00:27:46,790 --> 00:27:47,999
Units five and six are in.

716
00:27:48,000 --> 00:27:49,417
Down to a slow ooze here.

717
00:27:49,418 --> 00:27:50,794
Hold compressions.

718
00:27:54,381 --> 00:27:56,424
Looks like sinus.

719
00:27:56,425 --> 00:27:57,842
- And I got a weak carotid.
- OK.

720
00:27:57,843 --> 00:27:59,343
Cycle the BP.

721
00:27:59,344 --> 00:28:01,429
Better filling,
better squeeze.

722
00:28:01,430 --> 00:28:03,055
No seizure activity
on the EEG.

723
00:28:03,056 --> 00:28:04,557
That's progress.
That's progress.

724
00:28:04,558 --> 00:28:05,600
We're at five minutes.

725
00:28:05,601 --> 00:28:07,560
Uh, heart rate is 132.

726
00:28:07,561 --> 00:28:09,228
Uh, pulse ox 79%.

727
00:28:09,229 --> 00:28:11,105
Nazely, the APGAR?

728
00:28:11,106 --> 00:28:12,690
Um...

729
00:28:12,691 --> 00:28:14,817
1 off for color,
1 off for tone,

730
00:28:14,818 --> 00:28:17,403
1 off for respiration
with hypoxia, total of 7.

731
00:28:17,404 --> 00:28:18,779
Respiration score is
for observed breathing,

732
00:28:18,780 --> 00:28:20,198
not pulse ox.

733
00:28:20,199 --> 00:28:21,741
Sat of 80 is normal
at five minutes.

734
00:28:21,742 --> 00:28:23,201
With no crying,
she still gets 1 off.

735
00:28:23,202 --> 00:28:24,161
Yeah.

736
00:28:27,414 --> 00:28:28,497
Ah!

737
00:28:28,498 --> 00:28:30,082
She just scored
the winning point!

738
00:28:30,083 --> 00:28:32,377
APGAR of 8 is pretty normal.

739
00:28:35,672 --> 00:28:38,007
Holy shit. What did I miss?

740
00:28:38,008 --> 00:28:40,760
Eclampsia with status,
HELLP syndrome,

741
00:28:40,761 --> 00:28:43,930
cardiac arrest,
resuscitative hysterotomy.

742
00:28:43,931 --> 00:28:46,265
I was in the OR
with a septic twin C-section.

743
00:28:46,266 --> 00:28:47,516
Got your text 12 minutes ago.

744
00:28:47,517 --> 00:28:49,060
Shit happens fast down here.

745
00:28:49,061 --> 00:28:51,604
Resuscitative hysterotomy
in 36 seconds.

746
00:28:51,605 --> 00:28:53,898
- Impressive.
- BP's 102/64.

747
00:28:53,899 --> 00:28:55,107
Hemoglobin is up to 9.

748
00:28:55,108 --> 00:28:57,151
That'll do.

749
00:28:57,152 --> 00:28:58,569
NICU's sending a team down.

750
00:28:58,570 --> 00:29:00,905
We can take Mom.
You guys are rock stars.

751
00:29:00,906 --> 00:29:03,325
We like to be referred to
as crawlers of the night.

752
00:29:06,578 --> 00:29:07,954
If you're not careful,

753
00:29:07,955 --> 00:29:09,497
you're gonna get stuck
here all night.

754
00:29:09,498 --> 00:29:11,999
Nah, Henny said she'd
be here in 30 minutes.

755
00:29:12,000 --> 00:29:14,585
- How's Mom and baby?
- Whew.

756
00:29:14,586 --> 00:29:16,545
They're both gonna go upstairs.

757
00:29:16,546 --> 00:29:18,714
Good. You leaving now?

758
00:29:18,715 --> 00:29:20,383
Yeah, pretty soon.

759
00:29:20,384 --> 00:29:23,511
I gotta find Whitaker,
I gotta find Al-Hashimi,

760
00:29:23,512 --> 00:29:25,763
and I gotta find Langdon
before I leave.

761
00:29:25,764 --> 00:29:28,183
You missed Langdon.
He just checked out.

762
00:29:31,561 --> 00:29:32,688
Shit.

763
00:29:56,169 --> 00:29:57,586
Can I help you?

764
00:29:57,587 --> 00:30:01,132
Uh, yeah, I'm Dr. Langdon
from the ED.

765
00:30:01,133 --> 00:30:04,051
I was just, uh,
checking in on the status

766
00:30:04,052 --> 00:30:06,721
of someone we sent up here
earlier.

767
00:30:06,722 --> 00:30:09,348
Patient's name is, uh, Cohen.

768
00:30:09,349 --> 00:30:10,599
Let me check.

769
00:30:10,600 --> 00:30:11,892
What was she up here for?

770
00:30:11,893 --> 00:30:13,645
Uh, clean out
a nasty neck fash.

771
00:30:16,398 --> 00:30:18,065
Oh, yeah, she's good.

772
00:30:18,066 --> 00:30:21,193
She's in 4202,
recovering nicely.

773
00:30:21,194 --> 00:30:23,779
Great, great.

774
00:30:23,780 --> 00:30:26,699
I mean, she was--she was
in not-great shape earlier.

775
00:30:26,700 --> 00:30:28,826
It was a good catch.

776
00:30:28,827 --> 00:30:32,830
Saved her life, even if
we couldn't save her leg.

777
00:30:32,831 --> 00:30:35,791
Uh, was it below the knee?

778
00:30:35,792 --> 00:30:37,586
Unfortunately, it was above.

779
00:30:54,561 --> 00:30:57,688
My cell phone
and the building manager's.

780
00:30:57,689 --> 00:30:59,607
He can help if there's
any emergencies.

781
00:30:59,608 --> 00:31:01,734
Yeah,
what kind of emergencies?

782
00:31:01,735 --> 00:31:03,110
Whatever.

783
00:31:03,111 --> 00:31:04,111
And follow up with Duke

784
00:31:04,112 --> 00:31:05,112
in a couple days, yeah?

785
00:31:05,113 --> 00:31:06,155
Yeah.

786
00:31:06,156 --> 00:31:08,574
You, um--you sure about this?

787
00:31:08,575 --> 00:31:10,409
I trust you, Whitaker.

788
00:31:10,410 --> 00:31:12,161
Great.

789
00:31:12,162 --> 00:31:13,621
Any questions?

790
00:31:13,622 --> 00:31:16,707
Uh, when are you back, exactly?

791
00:31:16,708 --> 00:31:18,167
You know, I'll text you.

792
00:31:18,168 --> 00:31:20,003
I'm trying to keep my dates
kind of fluid.

793
00:31:21,421 --> 00:31:23,547
I think this is your ride.

794
00:31:23,548 --> 00:31:25,591
Yeah, uh, yes.

795
00:31:25,592 --> 00:31:28,135
I--I promise I'll check in
on your house tomorrow.

796
00:31:28,136 --> 00:31:29,596
Sounds good.

797
00:31:30,764 --> 00:31:32,473
- Hey.
- Hey.

798
00:31:32,474 --> 00:31:35,559
OK. Hey, Theo.

799
00:31:35,560 --> 00:31:37,395
You're up late, huh?

800
00:31:37,396 --> 00:31:38,688
What you got there?

801
00:31:41,608 --> 00:31:44,026
OK.

802
00:31:44,027 --> 00:31:45,694
He's been fussy all day.

803
00:31:45,695 --> 00:31:47,863
I think he's got
another tooth coming in.

804
00:31:47,864 --> 00:31:49,573
Aw, right on, big guy.

805
00:31:49,574 --> 00:31:52,868
Are you ready to get funky?

806
00:31:52,869 --> 00:31:53,870
Yeah?

807
00:32:13,849 --> 00:32:15,266
Hey.

808
00:32:15,267 --> 00:32:17,185
Any luck picking an elective?

809
00:32:18,687 --> 00:32:20,021
Don't know.

810
00:32:21,523 --> 00:32:23,650
Maybe I will go
into geriatrics.

811
00:32:25,235 --> 00:32:27,195
It's a smart choice.

812
00:32:30,949 --> 00:32:32,575
I know that life can be
challenging,

813
00:32:32,576 --> 00:32:33,951
especially when
it doesn't work out

814
00:32:33,952 --> 00:32:35,286
the way you expected.

815
00:32:35,287 --> 00:32:36,413
OK.

816
00:32:41,334 --> 00:32:42,793
I thought I would be married

817
00:32:42,794 --> 00:32:44,838
with two kids in college
by now.

818
00:32:46,173 --> 00:32:48,924
Maybe have some property
with a pond,

819
00:32:48,925 --> 00:32:51,094
and we could play hockey on it
in the wintertime.

820
00:32:53,263 --> 00:32:54,513
And yet look at me now.

821
00:32:54,514 --> 00:32:58,560
No wife, no kids, no pond.

822
00:33:02,063 --> 00:33:04,273
It's never too late.

823
00:33:04,274 --> 00:33:06,775
Do you really believe that?

824
00:33:06,776 --> 00:33:08,152
Yeah.

825
00:33:08,153 --> 00:33:09,862
Only for me, or for you too?

826
00:33:09,863 --> 00:33:11,489
OK.

827
00:33:11,490 --> 00:33:13,033
I see what you did there.

828
00:33:14,284 --> 00:33:16,953
Was that true, or something
you just said to make a point?

829
00:33:23,126 --> 00:33:25,795
Have you worked things out
with your mom?

830
00:33:28,089 --> 00:33:29,633
We're not talking.

831
00:33:32,928 --> 00:33:37,224
I am sorry that, um,
I let it distract me.

832
00:33:38,767 --> 00:33:40,434
She was treating me
like a child,

833
00:33:40,435 --> 00:33:41,770
and I was letting her.

834
00:33:47,025 --> 00:33:48,485
Have a good trip.

835
00:33:49,653 --> 00:33:50,779
Please be safe.

836
00:33:52,781 --> 00:33:55,199
We need you here.

837
00:33:55,200 --> 00:33:57,285
Even if you can be
a dick sometimes.

838
00:34:00,205 --> 00:34:01,373
Good luck.

839
00:34:02,749 --> 00:34:04,084
You too.

840
00:34:13,218 --> 00:34:15,344
Hey, I didn't think
you were still here.

841
00:34:15,345 --> 00:34:17,764
I was just talking
to the neurologist on call.

842
00:34:19,182 --> 00:34:20,975
And?

843
00:34:20,976 --> 00:34:24,311
We had a nice chat.

844
00:34:24,312 --> 00:34:26,981
She agrees I can work
with double coverage.

845
00:34:26,982 --> 00:34:29,400
That's not her call to make.

846
00:34:29,401 --> 00:34:30,776
You can't do anything critical

847
00:34:30,777 --> 00:34:32,278
where a five-second lapse
in consciousness

848
00:34:32,279 --> 00:34:34,030
could potentially
kill a patient.

849
00:34:35,907 --> 00:34:37,075
I agree.

850
00:34:40,579 --> 00:34:41,870
But 90% of our patients

851
00:34:41,871 --> 00:34:43,163
don't require
critical procedures.

852
00:34:43,164 --> 00:34:45,332
And the ones that do?

853
00:34:45,333 --> 00:34:47,710
Will be handled by
whomever is working with me.

854
00:34:47,711 --> 00:34:49,628
Unless they're also tied up
with a critical patient.

855
00:34:49,629 --> 00:34:51,005
What if it's a double
or triple trauma?

856
00:34:51,006 --> 00:34:53,007
- Robby, I can handle it.
- No, you can't.

857
00:34:53,008 --> 00:34:54,425
And I can't let you.

858
00:34:54,426 --> 00:34:55,843
I am fully capable
of handling--

859
00:34:55,844 --> 00:34:57,428
No, you are not
fully capable,

860
00:34:57,429 --> 00:34:58,805
and you know it.

861
00:35:02,601 --> 00:35:04,059
What do you want from me?

862
00:35:04,060 --> 00:35:05,185
I want what's best
for this department--

863
00:35:05,186 --> 00:35:06,645
patients and staff.

864
00:35:06,646 --> 00:35:08,897
Best-case scenario,
you get a handle on this,

865
00:35:08,898 --> 00:35:10,482
you're seizure-free
for six months,

866
00:35:10,483 --> 00:35:11,692
you get your
driver's license back,

867
00:35:11,693 --> 00:35:12,985
you are cleared to work.

868
00:35:12,986 --> 00:35:15,321
I am cleared
for my driver's license.

869
00:35:15,322 --> 00:35:17,489
You shouldn't be driving
at all like this.

870
00:35:17,490 --> 00:35:19,950
If you were a patient,
we would have to report you.

871
00:35:19,951 --> 00:35:21,535
I am not
your fucking patient.

872
00:35:21,536 --> 00:35:22,661
No, but I cannot let you work

873
00:35:22,662 --> 00:35:24,038
in my emergency department

874
00:35:24,039 --> 00:35:25,873
until you're fully capable
of doing so.

875
00:35:25,874 --> 00:35:27,583
That is not
your fucking call!

876
00:35:27,584 --> 00:35:29,126
You're fucking-A right,
that's my call!

877
00:35:29,127 --> 00:35:31,086
I'm trying to protect you
and my patients,

878
00:35:31,087 --> 00:35:32,421
and you know I'm right
about this.

879
00:35:32,422 --> 00:35:34,173
Oh, "my department,"
"my patients."

880
00:35:34,174 --> 00:35:35,674
All you fucking think about
is yourself!

881
00:35:35,675 --> 00:35:36,967
Do you hear yourself?

882
00:35:36,968 --> 00:35:38,010
You didn't rat out Langdon

883
00:35:38,011 --> 00:35:39,553
for stealing fucking drugs.

884
00:35:39,554 --> 00:35:41,138
No, but I kicked him
out of this department

885
00:35:41,139 --> 00:35:43,057
until he got the appropriate
help that he needs,

886
00:35:43,058 --> 00:35:44,933
and the same goes for you.

887
00:35:44,934 --> 00:35:46,560
You've got until Monday
to let the administration know,

888
00:35:46,561 --> 00:35:47,646
or I will.

889
00:35:54,778 --> 00:35:56,654
I am finished.

890
00:35:56,655 --> 00:35:58,406
Last chart.

891
00:35:59,574 --> 00:36:01,075
- You and me both.
- Really?

892
00:36:01,076 --> 00:36:02,535
Is this a thing?
I finished a while ago.

893
00:36:04,079 --> 00:36:05,872
I never want to hear
that fucking bell again.

894
00:36:10,460 --> 00:36:11,960
- Where's Dana?
- Not sure.

895
00:36:11,961 --> 00:36:13,504
A bunch of day shift
just headed to the roof

896
00:36:13,505 --> 00:36:14,713
to watch the fireworks.

897
00:36:14,714 --> 00:36:16,006
You want me to call her?

898
00:36:16,007 --> 00:36:17,467
No, that's OK.

899
00:36:19,386 --> 00:36:20,886
Yo.

900
00:36:20,887 --> 00:36:22,555
Thanks for your help in there.

901
00:36:24,474 --> 00:36:26,685
- Almost out?
- Yep, just about.

902
00:36:28,978 --> 00:36:30,729
Is this where you try
to talk me out of going?

903
00:36:30,730 --> 00:36:31,730
Me?

904
00:36:31,731 --> 00:36:33,524
No, not a chance.

905
00:36:33,525 --> 00:36:34,733
Why, are you having
second thoughts?

906
00:36:34,734 --> 00:36:35,734
- Nope.
- No?

907
00:36:35,735 --> 00:36:37,361
Nope.

908
00:36:37,362 --> 00:36:39,363
Don't have to convince me.

909
00:36:39,364 --> 00:36:40,698
I mean, it is a little strange
the only place

910
00:36:40,699 --> 00:36:42,241
you talked about going
is somewhere

911
00:36:42,242 --> 00:36:43,534
they used to drive buffalo
off a cliff to die.

912
00:36:43,535 --> 00:36:44,827
- Here it comes.
- I looked it up,

913
00:36:44,828 --> 00:36:46,537
and as far
as summer vacations go,

914
00:36:46,538 --> 00:36:48,288
it's not exactly
a holiday hotspot.

915
00:36:48,289 --> 00:36:51,417
I mean, what's in
the fucking gift shop, man?

916
00:36:51,418 --> 00:36:52,626
It's just one place
I'm going.

917
00:36:52,627 --> 00:36:54,211
As long as it's not the last.

918
00:36:54,212 --> 00:36:56,380
Don't be pulling a "Thelma
and Louise" out there.

919
00:36:56,381 --> 00:36:58,590
I am minutes from taking
a three-month vacation.

920
00:36:58,591 --> 00:37:00,134
When's the last time
you took any time off, Jack?

921
00:37:00,135 --> 00:37:01,928
Yeah, but I've dealt
with my demons.

922
00:37:03,304 --> 00:37:05,931
It's a process.

923
00:37:05,932 --> 00:37:08,642
You want to know why
I never killed myself?

924
00:37:08,643 --> 00:37:12,062
After what I saw,
lived through?

925
00:37:12,063 --> 00:37:15,608
Losing my leg, losing my wife?

926
00:37:16,901 --> 00:37:19,069
Because it comes
for all of us, man.

927
00:37:19,070 --> 00:37:20,279
You and I know it
more than most.

928
00:37:20,280 --> 00:37:21,989
We see it every shift,

929
00:37:21,990 --> 00:37:24,075
but we can't let ourselves
succumb to it.

930
00:37:25,201 --> 00:37:26,995
Yes, life can suck.

931
00:37:28,371 --> 00:37:30,414
It can be unbearable

932
00:37:30,415 --> 00:37:32,249
and--and brutal

933
00:37:32,250 --> 00:37:34,960
and ugly and heartbreaking.

934
00:37:34,961 --> 00:37:39,131
But it's also beautiful--
and hilarious.

935
00:37:39,132 --> 00:37:41,342
And that woman today...

936
00:37:44,387 --> 00:37:46,013
Her baby, they'd both be
in the morgue

937
00:37:46,014 --> 00:37:47,931
if you hadn't been here.

938
00:37:47,932 --> 00:37:49,767
That's us.
That's you and me.

939
00:37:49,768 --> 00:37:52,728
That's what we're here for.

940
00:37:52,729 --> 00:37:55,355
The most important things
I've ever done in my life

941
00:37:55,356 --> 00:37:58,025
have been in this hospital.

942
00:37:58,026 --> 00:38:00,486
Nothing will ever matter more
than what I've done

943
00:38:00,487 --> 00:38:03,406
in this hospital,
but it is killing me.

944
00:38:05,074 --> 00:38:07,201
You know how they say
that a part of you dies

945
00:38:07,202 --> 00:38:08,827
when you lose someone you love?

946
00:38:08,828 --> 00:38:11,205
I'm not convinced that
a part of you doesn't die

947
00:38:11,206 --> 00:38:13,373
every time you see
a fellow human pass.

948
00:38:13,374 --> 00:38:17,878
And I've seen
so many people die

949
00:38:17,879 --> 00:38:20,840
that I feel like it's leaching
something from my soul.

950
00:38:22,592 --> 00:38:24,594
Go on a cruise, man.

951
00:38:27,013 --> 00:38:29,848
Knock off this
helmetless motorcycle shit.

952
00:38:29,849 --> 00:38:31,934
Yeah, people talk.

953
00:38:31,935 --> 00:38:33,310
That's death-wish behavior.

954
00:38:33,311 --> 00:38:34,770
I'm tired of being
a role model.

955
00:38:34,771 --> 00:38:36,688
I'm tired of feeling
like you can't get ahead.

956
00:38:36,689 --> 00:38:38,440
I'm tired of feeling
like I'm drowning every day.

957
00:38:38,441 --> 00:38:39,733
I'm tired of all of it.

958
00:38:39,734 --> 00:38:40,943
You need to get away
for a while,

959
00:38:40,944 --> 00:38:42,361
and you need to get some help.

960
00:38:42,362 --> 00:38:45,740
You need this place
as much as it needs you.

961
00:38:50,203 --> 00:38:52,287
Am I fucked up?

962
00:38:52,288 --> 00:38:53,873
100%.

963
00:38:57,418 --> 00:38:59,628
But nobody works here
as long as you and me

964
00:38:59,629 --> 00:39:00,796
and doesn't get screwed up.

965
00:39:00,797 --> 00:39:03,966
You--you gotta find somebody

966
00:39:03,967 --> 00:39:06,636
to help you dance
through the darkness.

967
00:39:10,723 --> 00:39:12,350
Did you just make that up?

968
00:39:14,602 --> 00:39:16,186
Maybe it's a song lyric.

969
00:39:16,187 --> 00:39:17,771
I don't--
maybe my therapist said it.

970
00:39:17,772 --> 00:39:19,691
I don't know.

971
00:39:22,527 --> 00:39:23,944
Some dude just pulled up.

972
00:39:23,945 --> 00:39:25,947
Looks like he blew
half his face off.

973
00:39:28,825 --> 00:39:30,618
How can you not love
this place?

974
00:39:33,079 --> 00:39:36,498
Look, don't make me
look stupid.

975
00:39:36,499 --> 00:39:38,877
You come back to us
in one piece.

976
00:39:42,297 --> 00:39:43,755
I'm still your
emergency contact,

977
00:39:43,756 --> 00:39:46,092
and I do not want
to be contacted.

978
00:39:48,469 --> 00:39:49,678
All right, night crawlers,

979
00:39:49,679 --> 00:39:50,889
what the hell's going on
out here?

980
00:39:56,477 --> 00:39:57,811
25-year-old man...

981
00:39:57,812 --> 00:39:59,104
history,

982
00:39:59,105 --> 00:40:00,356
no meds, no allergies.

983
00:41:26,776 --> 00:41:28,735
<i>More than 2,000 years ago,</i>

984
00:41:28,736 --> 00:41:30,904
the Chinese were throwing
bamboo into fire

985
00:41:30,905 --> 00:41:32,906
to make explosions.

986
00:41:32,907 --> 00:41:34,449
They went on
to invent gunpowder.

987
00:41:34,450 --> 00:41:36,577
And boom! The rest is history.

988
00:41:38,246 --> 00:41:41,373
They had chemicals to get
the different colors, you know?

989
00:41:41,374 --> 00:41:44,126
Sodium gives you yellow,
strontium gives you red,

990
00:41:44,127 --> 00:41:47,212
and barium is green.

991
00:41:47,213 --> 00:41:50,717
Who knew chemistry could be
so damn pretty?

992
00:42:59,702 --> 00:43:01,495
- Hey.
- Hey.

993
00:43:01,496 --> 00:43:03,914
- I thought you'd left already.
- On my way out.

994
00:43:03,915 --> 00:43:07,876
Hey, I'm sorry that
I didn't find the time today

995
00:43:07,877 --> 00:43:09,044
to have that conversation.

996
00:43:09,045 --> 00:43:10,378
Yeah, that's all right.

997
00:43:10,379 --> 00:43:12,297
Seems like you
didn't really want to.

998
00:43:12,298 --> 00:43:13,549
I didn't.

999
00:43:16,552 --> 00:43:18,011
Did you?

1000
00:43:18,012 --> 00:43:20,347
Uh...

1001
00:43:20,348 --> 00:43:23,141
yeah, actually.

1002
00:43:23,142 --> 00:43:26,228
Look, I'm doing the work.

1003
00:43:26,229 --> 00:43:28,688
I'm--I've been sober 186 days.

1004
00:43:28,689 --> 00:43:30,941
I'm going to meetings.
I'm taking the drug tests.

1005
00:43:30,942 --> 00:43:33,152
- That's good.
- And you're still riding me.

1006
00:43:36,197 --> 00:43:39,616
What would have happened
if I'd paralyzed that guy?

1007
00:43:39,617 --> 00:43:41,284
I don't know.

1008
00:43:41,285 --> 00:43:42,869
What would have happened
if I hadn't been here today?

1009
00:43:42,870 --> 00:43:44,579
You'd still be
questioning yourself.

1010
00:43:44,580 --> 00:43:46,331
Now you know you can do it.
You're welcome.

1011
00:43:46,332 --> 00:43:47,916
Oh, so that's--
that's how you teach now?

1012
00:43:47,917 --> 00:43:49,876
Sometimes.

1013
00:43:49,877 --> 00:43:52,212
You know who I saw in rehab?

1014
00:43:52,213 --> 00:43:54,881
I saw a bunch of guys
just like you.

1015
00:43:54,882 --> 00:43:56,174
The only difference is,

1016
00:43:56,175 --> 00:43:59,302
they've accepted
that they need help.

1017
00:43:59,303 --> 00:44:01,346
I think you're afraid
to admit that

1018
00:44:01,347 --> 00:44:04,015
the mighty Dr. Robinavitch
isn't perfect.

1019
00:44:04,016 --> 00:44:06,059
Oh, I never claimed
to be perfect.

1020
00:44:06,060 --> 00:44:09,312
No, but you expect it
of yourself,

1021
00:44:09,313 --> 00:44:11,773
and it's not realistic, man.

1022
00:44:11,774 --> 00:44:14,109
How can any of us live up
to your standards

1023
00:44:14,110 --> 00:44:15,778
if you can't even do it?

1024
00:44:17,238 --> 00:44:20,198
You need help, Robby.

1025
00:44:20,199 --> 00:44:21,909
You need help.

1026
00:44:24,787 --> 00:44:25,913
Finished?

1027
00:44:27,165 --> 00:44:29,541
You don't gotta be honest
with me, man.

1028
00:44:29,542 --> 00:44:31,502
At least be honest
with yourself.

1029
00:44:47,059 --> 00:44:49,436
She is due for a new bottle.

1030
00:44:49,437 --> 00:44:52,148
I was hoping to get her some
formula before I clocked out.

1031
00:44:53,900 --> 00:44:56,276
I'll stay with her.

1032
00:44:56,277 --> 00:44:57,486
Thanks.

1033
00:44:59,780 --> 00:45:01,990
Why are you--will you hit
those lights on your way out?

1034
00:45:01,991 --> 00:45:05,035
- Yep.
- Why are you crying?

1035
00:45:05,036 --> 00:45:07,621
Why are you crying, little one?

1036
00:45:07,622 --> 00:45:10,207
You're OK. You're safe.

1037
00:45:10,208 --> 00:45:12,418
Yeah, you're not alone.

1038
00:45:19,383 --> 00:45:21,927
Yeah, you're OK.

1039
00:45:21,928 --> 00:45:25,222
Do you need to be
swaddled again?

1040
00:45:25,223 --> 00:45:26,973
Is that it?

1041
00:45:26,974 --> 00:45:28,934
I can do that. Look.

1042
00:45:28,935 --> 00:45:31,519
Aww.

1043
00:45:31,520 --> 00:45:35,273
I wish somebody
would swaddle me.

1044
00:45:35,274 --> 00:45:37,692
Yes, I do.

1045
00:45:37,693 --> 00:45:39,695
